checked_ok:
A mixed box keeps its mark while its record lives (the chain path) and after it goes (mixedLeaves). It survives:
- a restart: Withdrawing.origin `mixed` reads back through isHistoryClass;
- a lock: store.get and set throw (private-store.ts:136-157), so nothing is half-written, and every new write sits in one update;
- a bring run: it runs no sortOut, so the record stays.
It is lost only where a leaf isn't listed when its record goes (a lagging listing, or a pool missing from the read set), as 1.9.1's `leaves` were. The due-time run then asks Koios and marks it again; Bring every box back now gives (d).

